# Canonical Design Artifacts

When the user asks to output, finalize, or update a design/plan artifact:

- Write it under `docs/` using `docs/TEMPLATE.md`.
- Maintain one canonical document per cohesive problem, even across repositories.
- Split only independently designed and versioned problems into separate documents.
- Update the existing artifact instead of creating `v2`, `latest`, or `final` copies.
- Record settled decisions, non-goals, current evidence, contracts, risks, and failures.
- Use repo-scoped ticket IDs: `API-*`, `APP-*`, and `INFRA-*`.
- Size each ticket for one agent run and one reviewable PR, normally in one repository.
- Give every ticket dependencies, safe parallel work, acceptance criteria, tests, and handoff outputs.
- Define ordering through a dependency graph and delivery gates; numbering alone is not order.
- Keep diagrams in the appendix and link to them from the relevant main section.
- Prefer Mermaid; store large external diagrams under `docs/assets/<artifact-slug>/`.
- Include an agent-handoff section naming the ticket, repository, dependencies, and contract inputs.
- Mark an artifact `canonical` only when no open question blocks implementation.

Do not silently invent unresolved product decisions. Mark them clearly and ask the user when
the choice would materially alter architecture, scope, security, cost, or user behavior.
